# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true on Windows makes every LF-written file
# show as modified while the committed blob is byte-identical. On 2026-08-26 that
# noise hid the truth: `git status` showed 40 modified files of which only 17 had
# any content change -- including a 92-line skill edit from a parallel session.
# Noise that conceals real changes is a safety problem, not a cosmetic one.

* text=auto

# Executed on Linux servers and by Git Bash. CRLF here yields
# "$'\r': command not found" and a broken hook.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Windows-only hosts. Stated explicitly rather than left to the platform default.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.vbs   text eol=crlf
